---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "/news/"
pageId: "news"
title: "News"
description: "What the movement is doing, and the prices in the news — each with its publisher and its date."
---
{% import "partials/news-cards.njk" as nc %}
{#- Markup taken from design-source/pages/news.html. CONTENT.md marks this
    page's copy "inline (draft)", so the export supplies both; only asset
    references and routes are rewritten. Do not re-author.

    Exception, founder-approved under UNP-82 v1 §4b: Cost Watch is no longer a
    hand-curated reading list of third-party articles. It renders the register's
    own `placement=news-feed` rows, so every entry is a sourced, dated figure
    under the same rule as the rest of the site. The export's three hardcoded
    links and its "inclusion isn't endorsement" note went with that model.

    Exception, founder-approved under N1: this is now a split landing. Both
    columns are first-class — each carries its own head, its own one-line
    intro, its own filter and its own link to the full list — and the single
    combined intro sentence in the introband is gone, because an intro that
    describes two things describes neither. Column intros, and the Reported
    definition, are founder-approved copy. -#}
<!-- SECTION: news.News — title -->
<div class="titleband" data-screen-label="News — title"><h1><span class="u-1">News</span></h1></div>
<div class="introband">
  <h2>What&rsquo;s moving — ours and the world&rsquo;s.</h2>
</div>

<div class="newswrap">
  <!-- SECTION: news.Updates -->
  <div class="updates" data-screen-label="Updates">
    <h3 class="colhead">Uncost news</h3>
    <p class="cwsub">What the movement is doing, dated and honest, including the updates that aren&rsquo;t good news.</p>
{#- N5 keyword filter, one per column, same progressive-enhancement pattern as
    /receipts/: the bar ships hidden and only /js/keyword-filter.js reveals it,
    so with JS off every item renders and no dead control is shown. -#}
    <div class="rfilter" data-keyword-filter data-filter-for="news-uncost" data-filter-noun="updates" hidden>
      <label for="ufilter-q">Filter these updates</label>
      <input id="ufilter-q" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Try &ldquo;policy&rdquo; or &ldquo;repository&rdquo;&hellip;">
      <span class="rfilter-count" data-filter-count></span>
    </div>
    <div id="news-uncost">
{% for item in news | take(3) %}
      {{ nc.update(item, 4, true) }}
{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="morelink"><a href="/news/uncost/">All Uncost news &rarr;</a></p>
    <p class="u-96" id="rss">More updates arrive as the movement launches. Prefer a feed? <a href="/news/feed.xml">Subscribe by RSS</a> &mdash; every update, no algorithm in between.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION: news.Cost Watch -->
  <aside class="costwatch" data-screen-label="Cost Watch">
    <h3 class="colhead">Cost Watch</h3>
    <p class="cwsub">Prices in the news, with the publisher and the date attached. Not receipts &mdash; verified figures live in <a href="/receipts/">The Receipts</a>.</p>
    <p class="cwdef"><b>Reported</b> &mdash; a price or cost figure as published by the linked source, with its date. Cost Watch is a watch list, not a receipt; verified figures live in <a href="/receipts/">The Receipts</a>.</p>
    <div class="rfilter" data-keyword-filter data-filter-for="news-costwatch" data-filter-noun="items" hidden>
      <label for="cfilter-q">Filter these items</label>
      <input id="cfilter-q" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Try &ldquo;gasoline&rdquo; or &ldquo;BLS&rdquo;&hellip;">
      <span class="rfilter-count" data-filter-count></span>
    </div>
    <div id="news-costwatch">
{% for row in register.newsFeed | take(5) %}
      {{ nc.costwatch(row, 4) }}
{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="morelink"><a href="/news/cost-watch/">All Cost Watch &rarr;</a></p>
    <p class="u-97">Checked {{ register.lastChecked }}. Every figure here has a <a href="/receipts/#register">receipt</a>.</p>
  </aside>
</div>
<script src="/js/keyword-filter.js" defer></script>
